m darkness of the 41st millennium, Sergeant Leonis Mavik and his battle-hardened squad of Space Marines face a threat that defies comprehension. Tasked with purging a hive world overrun by a cult worshiping a shard of unimaginable Warp-tainted power, they uncover a secret that shakes their faith and challenges their loyalty. As the shard\'s whispers twist minds and reality alike, Leonis makes a fateful choice to wield its power, risking his humanity to save the hive. But in the Imperium of Man, survival often comes at a cost. With the Inquisition breathing down their necks and the shadow of the Warp looming ever closer, the squad must navigate the razor\'s edge between duty and damnation. Will their bonds endure, or will the shard\'s influence shatter their brotherhood forever? "The Shard\'s Shadow" is a gripping Warhammer 40K novel that blends the ferocity of battle with psychological and cosmic horror, exploring themes of corruption, sacrifice, and the price of survival in a galaxy consumed by endless war. For fans of Warhammer 40K, dark sci-fi, and intense moral dilemmas, this is a story that lingers long after the last bolter round is fired. Perfect for readers who enjoy: Warhammer 40K\'s dark and brutal universe. Psychological horror interwoven with visceral battle scenes. Complex, morally ambiguous characters navigating impossible choices. Themes of loyalty, corruption, and the cost of victory. "A gripping descent into the heart of darkness. \'The Shard\'s Shadow\' is the perfect blend of brutal warfare and psychological horror. A must-read for any Warhammer 40K fan." - T. Gray, sci-fi author "Torrin Nightflare captures the grimdark essence of Warhammer 40K with stunning precision. This story will keep you on edge until the final page." - M. Shaw, editor of Tactical Fiction Review "Bold, haunting, and unforgettable. \'The Shard\'s Shadow\' explores what it truly means to fight for survival in the 41st millennium." - R. Vega, Warhammer lore enthusiast "Nightflar\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user\'s search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'description': 'Structured relevance judgment for a single (query, book) pair.\n\nThe ``reason`` field is mandatory so every judgment can be audited\nor used for fine-tuning the judge model later.', 'properties': {'score': {'description': 'Relevance score: 0 = not relevant, 1 = somewhat relevant, 2 = highly relevant.', 'title': 'Score', 'type': 'integer'}, 'reason': {'description': 'Concise explanation (1-3 sentences) justifying the score. Used for auditing and debugging.', 'title': 'Reason', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['score', 'reason'], 'title': 'RelevanceScore', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'RelevanceScore', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
