ood Lane\n\nDescription:\nSome houses don't just shelter evil-they hunger for it. When the Morrison family moves into their dream home, they have no idea they've just become prey. The house on Blackwood Lane has stood empty for decades, and there's a reason why: it feeds on souls. What begins as strange noises and cold spots quickly escalates into a nightmare of supernatural terror. Doors that lock themselves. Shadows that move on their own. Whispers in the walls that know your darkest secrets. And something ancient and malevolent that grows stronger with each passing night. The house is alive. The house is hungry. And it won't let them leave. As the family struggles to survive, they uncover the horrifying truth: every family that's lived here before them has disappeared without a trace. The house doesn't just haunt its victims-it consumes them, absorbing their essence to feed its insatiable appetite. Now the Morrisons must fight for their lives against an enemy that knows their every fear. With nowhere to run and no one who believes them, the family must confront the demonic force that dwells within the walls. But the house has been waiting for them. It knows their weaknesses. It feeds on their terror. And it will stop at nothing to claim their souls. A story of: Supernatural horror and demonic possession Family bonds tested by unimaginable evil Psychological terror that builds with every page Ancient evil awakening after decades of slumber The fight for survival against impossible odds Perfect for readers who love: Haunted house horror Supernatural thrillers Demonic possession stories Psychological horror Stories about evil that lurks in everyday places Warning: Contains graphic horror content and intense supernatural terror.\n\nEvaluate whether this book satisfies the user's search intent.\n\nReturn:\n\n* score (0, 1, or 2)\n* concise reason\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'descri